## The fate map (computed EQS-1060; accords the filed EQS-1036 windows exactly)
A structural material built today rides the filed clock: its split can only rise,
by ln rho_inf = 0.0945841102 at most. That one fact partitions ALL structural
densities into five fates:
- GAP-HOLD, bulk < 342.6: never enters the shell at any future epoch.
- PENDING ENTRY, 342.6-500.1: enters in the future (crossing epoch set by density).
- PERMANENT SHELL, 500.1-15,483.9: in the shell today and at the terminal state.
- PENDING EXIT, 15,483.9-22,604.3: in the shell today, exits before the terminal.
- ABOVE SHELL, > 22,604.3: outside, on the far side.

